From: WorkBuddy <noreply@workbuddy.local>
Subject: [PATCH] mt_wifi: raise 5G Single-SKU tx power limit to 29dBm

The MT7986 AX6000 boards (Ruijie RG-X60 Pro / RG-X60 / EW-6000GX Pro) run with
Single-SKU power limit disabled (SKUenable=0), so the 5G tx power is taken
from the EEPROM country power table, which caps 5G at 26dBm.

This patch fills the built-in Single-SKU power limit table (Sku_01, selected
by SkuTableIdx=0) with 29dBm for every 5G channel/rate, so the 5G band power
limit becomes 29dBm once Single-SKU is enabled for band 1 only
(SKUenable=0;1, see mt7986-ax6000.dbdc.b1.dat in the wifi-profile package).

Only the 'Band: 5G' section is modified; the 2.4G section and all other SKU /
Backoff tables are left untouched, so 2.4G tx power stays on the EEPROM value.

Note: include/txpwr/PowerLimit_mt7915.h is the table actually compiled into
mt_wifi.ko (the OpenWrt build does not re-run data2h); txpwr/sku_tables/
Sku_01.dat is updated in the same way to keep the two in sync.

--- a/mt_wifi/include/txpwr/PowerLimit_mt7915.h	2026-10-20 18:50:23.305933600 +0800
+++ b/mt_wifi/include/txpwr/PowerLimit_mt7915.h	2026-10-20 18:50:24.433852600 +0800
@@ -18,112 +18,112 @@
 "	"
 "# 5G Channel CCK OFDM BW20 (HT/VHT) BW40 (HT/VHT) BW80 (HT/VHT) BW160 (HT/VHT) RU26 RU52 RU106 RU242 RU484 RU996 RU996X2	"
